[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station gauging a natural catchment. Ice build up can occur at the station. GENERAL: Velocity area station, 46m wide. Stable bedrock control. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2024 (WINFAP Files v13). STATION HYDROMETRY: Cableway present. All flows contained, rating curve well defined. Multiple peak flow ratings across period of record. FLOW RECORD: Extreme low temperatures can cause ice build up and hence erroneous flow values, e.g. Dec 2001 - Jan 2002. FLOW REGIME: Flows are natural.
CATCHMENT,Mountainous steeply sloping catchment. Mostly impermeable bedrock, metamorphic, two thirds overlain by superficial deposits. Land use mainly rough grazing with some forestry.
Qmed Suitability,Rating well supported by gaugings to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Flows are contained and the rating is informed by flood gaugings.
[END]
